  "body": "## What changed\n\nMachine files accept `tooling.reserved` entries.\nEach entry reserves a number, a name, or both for `probe` or `tool_setter`.\nThe reader and validator refuse malformed entries by key.\nStored projects retain the reservations.\n\nNew cutting tools skip reserved numbers.\nA probe takes a declared probe pocket.\nTool edits and library imports refuse incompatible reserved numbers or names.\nVerification and posting also refuse old unsafe assignments.\nThe existing GUI, script, and MCP commands use these checks.\nTool number zero remains refused.\n\nThe standalone post CLI checks its input before it creates or replaces output.\nIt retains the loaded tool across sections.\nA new TOOL needs its own declared kind.\nA stream with no tool selector cannot post motion on a machine with reservations.\nIndexed lookups keep the checks bounded for long streams.\n\nA machine that omits the field reserves nothing.\nNo shipped machine file reserves a pocket in this PR (see \"Review round 2\").\n\n### Project file version 77\n\nA stored machine can hold `reserved_tools`. `PROJECT_VERSION` steps from 76 to 77.\nAn older reader refuses a v77 file. It cannot drop the reservation and post a cutting tool at a reserved pocket.\nThe step is a pure step-up: a v76 file opens with no change.\nThe rule entries are in `crates/app/src/project/file.rs` and `crates/app/src/project/apply.rs`.\n\nPR #3485 also asks for a version step. Main is at 76 now, so this PR takes 77.\nIf #3485 merges first and takes 77, this PR takes 78 at its refresh.\n\n## Cause\n\nTool allocation considered only document numbers.\nMachine files could not protect a probe pocket or a control-managed tool name.\nThe app and standalone post paths had no reservation check.\n\n## Review round 2 (second review of `e6881bb0a`)\n\n- Blocker, version step: done (above).\n- T99 provenance: removed. I found no public Tormach document that names T99 as the probe pocket.\n  The earlier #362 research calls T99 a convention of the PathPilot probing screens only.\n  The 18 Tormach files are identical to `main` again. A follow-up can add T99 with a cited document.\n- `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`: the `tooling.reserved` row is added.\n- MCP text: the `add_tool` description now says that the number skips the machine's reservations.\n  It changes in `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`, `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` and `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`.\n- Body: refreshed. Parent #3157 merged, so the stack note and the parent's screenshots are removed.\n\n## Screenshots\n\nThis PR changes no UI file. No screenshot applies.\n\n## Tests on the final head\n\nFinal head: `3b5f359ff`. Base: `upstream/main` (merge-tree with the current main is clean).\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` | 152 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 7.3 min |\n| `cargo xtask gate light --base upstream/main` | 3 steps, 0 failed |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings` | passed |\n| `example_catalog` | 37 passed, 4 ignored |\n| `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` | 1 passed each |\n| `golden_cl` | 33 passed |\n| `continuous_4axis_part` | 10 passed |\n| `mcp_doc_drift` | 6 passed |\n\nHeavy lanes: not run. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" (#3556) does not require them for a P6 PR.\n\n### Pins and mutation proof (round 2)\n\n| Pin | Mutation | Mutated | Restored |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `saved_machine_reservations_need_the_v77_reader` (`crates/app/tests/tool_reservations_version.rs`) | `PROJECT_VERSION` back to 76 | RED at line 26 | GREEN |\n| `a_v76_machine_steps_up_with_no_reservation` (same file) | - | - | GREEN |\n| `shipped_machines_reserve_no_pocket_without_a_cited_manual` (`crates/post/tests/tool_reservations.rs`) | T99 put back in `tormach-24r.mch` | RED at line 98 | GREEN |\n\n`shipped_machines_reserve_no_pocket_without_a_cited_manual` replaces `shipped_tormach_mills_reserve_t99_for_the_probe`.\n`deburr_chord_width` asserted the saved version as exactly 76. It now asserts at least 76, which keeps its intent.\n\n### Earlier pins (round 1, unchanged)\n\nThe 30 other reservation pins pass in the quick gate. Each failed at runtime before its fix.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pin names</summary>\n\n`crates/app/tests/tool_reservations.rs`\n\n- `added_cutter_skips_probe_pocket_and_probe_takes_it`\n- `setting_cutter_to_reserved_pocket_refuses_by_name`\n- `adding_cutter_with_reserved_probe_name_refuses_by_name`\n- `importing_cutter_skips_probe_pocket_and_probe_takes_it`\n- `existing_cutting_tool_in_probe_pocket_blocks_verification`\n- `existing_cutting_tool_in_probe_pocket_blocks_post_stream`\n\n`crates/app/tests/tool_reservations_extra.rs`\n\n- `retyping_probe_in_reserved_pocket_as_cutter_refuses`\n- `retyping_probe_with_reserved_name_as_cutter_refuses`\n- `importing_explicit_reserved_number_for_cutter_refuses`\n- `generic_machine_keeps_first_cutter_at_t1_and_accepts_probe_word`\n- `existing_cutting_tool_with_reserved_name_blocks_verification`\n- `existing_cutting_tool_with_reserved_name_blocks_post_stream`\n- `machine_validator_names_a_bad_reservation`\n\n`crates/post/tests/tool_reservations.rs`\n\n- `malformed_reserved_tool_numbers_refuse_by_key`\n- `malformed_reserved_tool_entries_refuse_by_key`\n- `duplicate_reserved_tool_numbers_and_names_refuse_by_key`\n- `reserved_tools_survive_stored_machine_round_trip`\n- `an_old_machine_has_no_reserved_tools`\n- `invalid_stored_reservations_make_machine_insane`\n\n`crates/post/tests/tool_reservations_cli.rs`\n\n- `standalone_post_refuses_cutter_in_reserved_probe_pocket_before_writing`\n- `standalone_post_keeps_existing_output_when_probe_pocket_is_used_for_cutting`\n- `standalone_post_refuses_cutter_with_reserved_probe_name`\n- `standalone_post_refuses_reserved_tool_without_stated_kind`\n- `standalone_post_allows_stated_touch_probe_in_reserved_pocket`\n- `standalone_post_does_not_reuse_previous_probe_kind_for_unknown_tool`\n- `standalone_post_allows_probe_kind_stated_after_tool`\n- `standalone_post_refuses_probe_changed_to_cutter_inside_section`\n- `standalone_post_refuses_cutting_with_reserved_probe_reused_without_new_tool`\n- `standalone_post_refuses_cutting_without_any_tool_selector_on_reserved_machine`\n- `standalone_post_allows_probe_reused_across_sections_without_repeated_tool`\n\n</details>\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj`: only `\"version\": 76` changes to `77` (regenerated with `WRITE_GOLDEN=1`). The T99 entry from round 1 is gone.\n- No NC, CL or catalog program changes.\n  The regeneration also rewrote `examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.nc` with last-digit A rounding steps on this host.\n  The suite permits that step, so I kept the committed `.nc`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Physical machines, tool changers, or controller sessions.\n- Named tool-call execution on a Siemens control.\n- An older build that opens a v77 file. The pin proves the version step and the refusal of a newer version.\n- Full release tier and pixel snapshot lanes.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3485 also steps the project version (see \"Project file version 77\").\n- #3160, #3058, and #3057 touch `crates/app/src/lib.rs` at other module declarations. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: high\n\nProcess change: yes (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`)\n\nChangelog: Cutting tools skip reserved probe pockets and cannot use reserved tool names. Project files step to version 77; older builds refuse them.\n\nFixes #2604\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
